<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/2nd-century-bce">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Vercellae</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">101 BCE</span> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cimbrian-war">Cimbrian War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Vercellae was fought in 101 BCE on the Raudine Plain in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>, where Roman armies under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaius-marius">Gaius Marius</a> and Quintus Lutatius Catulus destroyed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cimbri">Cimbri</a>. Coming a year after Marius's victory over the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/teutones">Teutones</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aix-en-provence">Aquae Sextiae</a>, it ended the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cimbrian-war">Cimbrian War</a>, which had threatened Italy since the Roman disaster at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/orange-vaucluse">Arausio</a> in 105 BCE.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-vercellae.jpg" alt="Battle of Vercellae" width="320" height="350" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Giovanni Battista Tiepolo · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tiepolo_Vercellae.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
